# Lenovo ThinkCentre M920q Tiny — i5-8500T (6c/6t, 35W), 16GB, 256GB SSD.
# Ubuntu Server 26.04.1. Added 2026-09-15.
#
# **Its day job is browser testing**, not inference: Firefox and WebKit on
# x86-64 Linux for the dashboard suite, which is the one thing no other box in
# the estate can run (dashboard/plans/browser-matrix.md). That is why the role
# below is `controller` and not `compute`.
#
# **Role, deliberately.** `controller` means "never used for inference, sends
# only heartbeats" (docs/roles.md). A `compute` node is eligible for model
# scheduling, and a model landing on this box mid-Playwright-run would compete
# for the same six cores and make the browser timings meaningless — the
# measurement would move because of something that has nothing to do with the
# dashboard. Same reasoning pi1 records for itself one file over, from the other
# direction: the box has another job and inference would take it down.
#
# Promoting it later is two words here plus `just auto-load-model lenovo1`.
# Worth knowing what that would buy first: 16GB with no GPU puts it at CPU-only
# inference, which docs/frontier-hardware-2026.md measures as well under the
# 15–30 tok/s an agent needs to feel responsive. beelink1 has the GPU and mac1
# has the memory bandwidth; this box has neither.
#
# **`llm` is in FEATURES even though the role is controller**, and that is not a
# contradiction: NODE_FEATURES are Cargo features, the crate's `default` is
# empty, and `${NODE_FEATURES:-llm}` in the justfile substitutes `llm` for an
# unset value anyway — so there is no way to ask for "no capabilities" here.
#
# **What that costs, measured rather than assumed: llama-server IS installed.**
# The gate at `justfile:465` is on `auto-load-model`, not on the install, so the
# install script lays down `/opt/llama.cpp/llama-server` (41MB) whenever `llm` is
# in the feature list, whatever the role. Nothing starts it — verified after
# provisioning: no llama process, and the agent's cgroup holds only
# `/home/jonno/agent`. So it is 41MB of idle disk and a rebuild saved if the role
# is ever flipped to `compute`.
NODE_HOST=192.168.1.47
NODE_USER=jonno
NODE_OS=linux
NODE_ROLE=controller
NODE_FEATURES=llm
# Pinned rather than discovered, exactly as mac1.env is and for the same reason:
# this box is on the Velop and pi1 is on the Orbi, and mDNS across the two meshes
# is not trustworthy — infrastructure/network.md documents `pi1.local` failing to
# resolve while `ssh pi1` worked. Revisit after orbi-switch-plan.md.
COORDINATOR_IP=192.168.1.103
